   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *          functionalities of the Reset and clock control (RCC) peripheral:
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *           + Internal/external clocks, PLL, CSS and MCO configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *           + System, AHB and APB busses clocks configuration
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *           + Peripheral clocks configuration
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****  @verbatim
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****  ===============================================================================
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****                       ##### RCC specific features #####
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****  ===============================================================================
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****     [..]  
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       After reset the device is running from Internal High Speed oscillator 
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (HSI 16MHz) with Flash 0 wait state, Flash prefetch buffer, D-Cache 
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       and I-Cache are disabled, and all peripherals are off except internal
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       SRAM, Flash and JTAG.
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) There is no prescaler on High speed (AHB) and Low speed (APB) busses;
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****           all peripherals mapped on these busses are running at HSI speed.
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) The clock for all peripherals is switched off, except the SRAM and FLASH.
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) All GPIOs are in input floating state, except the JTAG pins which
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****           are assigned to be used for debug purpose.
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****     [..]          
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       Once the device started from reset, the user application has to:
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the clock source to be used to drive the System clock
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc9hYLCi.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****           (if the application needs higher frequency/performance)
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the System clock frequency and Flash settings  
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the AHB and APB busses prescalers
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) Enable the clock for the peripheral(s) to be used
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the clock source(s) for peripherals which clocks are not
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****           derived from the System clock (I2S, RTC, ADC, USB OTG FS/SDIO/RNG)
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****  @endverbatim    
