 357:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c **** /**
 358:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @brief  Enables or disables the Internal High Speed oscillator (HSI).
 359:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @note   The HSI is stopped by hardware when entering STOP and STANDBY modes.
 360:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         It is used (enabled by hardware) as system clock source after startup
 361:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         from Reset, wakeup from STOP and STANDBY mode, or in case of failure
 362:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         of the HSE used directly or indirectly as system clock (if the Clock
 363:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         Security System CSS is enabled).             
 364:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @note   HSI can not be stopped if it is used as system clock source. In this case,
 365:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         you have to select another source of the system clock then stop the HSI.  
 366:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @note   After enabling the HSI, the application software should wait on HSIRDY
 367:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         flag to be set indicating that HSI clock is stable and can be used as
 368:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         system clock source.  
 369:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @param  NewState: new state of the HSI.
 370:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *          This parameter can be: ENABLE or DISABLE.
 371:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @note   When the HSI is stopped, HSIRDY flag goes low after 6 HSI oscillator
 372:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   *         clock cycles.  
 373:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   * @retval None
 374:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_rcc.c ****   */
